{
  "title": "Unicompartmental Knee Replacement",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/5020/unicompartmental-knee-replacement",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 14 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Unicompartmental Knee Arthroplasty is a surgical option for knee arthritis when only one compartment of the knee is involved.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The procedure can be performed for isolated medial compartment, isolated lateral compartment or isolated patellofemoral osteoarthritis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The most common reasons for conversion to a total knee arthroplasty are the progression of osteoarthritis and aseptic loosening.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "5% of surgeries where knee arthroplasty is indicated are unicompartmental knee replacements",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "medial compartment is most common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Types of implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fixed-bearing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "historical standard of care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mobile-bearing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pros",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "weightbearing through the meniscus increases conformity and contact without increasing constraint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decrease in wear pattern",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "excellent survivorship out to the second decade",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cons",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "technically demanding",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bearings can dislocate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Advantages",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Compared to TKA",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "faster rehabilitation and quicker recovery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "less blood loss",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "less morbidity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "less expensive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lower rates of PJI, wound complications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "preservation of normal kinematics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "theory is that retaining ACL, PCL and other compartments leads to more normal knee kinematics",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "smaller incision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "less post-operative pain leading to shorter hospital stays",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Compared to osteotomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "faster rehabilitation and quicker recovery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "improved cosmesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "higher initial success rate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fewer short-term complications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lasts longer",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "easier to convert to a TKA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Indications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "controversial and vary widely",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "as an alternative to total knee arthroplasty or osteotomy for unicompartmental disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "classicaly reserved for older (>60), lower-demand, and thin (<82 kg) patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "6% of patient's meet the above criteria with no contraindications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "new effort to expand indications to include younger patients and patients with more moderate arthrosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Contraindications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**inflammatory arthritis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**ACL deficiency**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "absolute contraindication for lateral UKA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "controversial for medial fixed-bearing and for mobile-bearing UKA",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**fixed varus deformity > 10 degrees**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**fixed valgus deformity >5 degrees**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "restricted motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "arc of motion < 90°",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "flexion contracture of > 5-10°",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "previous meniscectomy in other compartment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**tricompartmental arthritis** (diffuse or global pain)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "younger high activity patients and heavy laborers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "grade IV patellofemoral chondrosis (anterior knee pain)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Procedural tips",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "avoid overcorrections",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "undercorrect the mechanical axis by 2-3 degrees",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "overcorrection places excess load on unresurfaced compartment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "remove osteophytes (peripheral and notch)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "resect minimal bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "avoid extensive releases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "avoid edge loading",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "prevent tibial spine impingement with proper mediolateral placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "avoid making a varus tibial cut which increases the chance for loosening",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "use caution when placing the proximal tibial guide pins to avoid stress fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "correct varus deformity to 1-5 degrees of valgus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Aseptic loosening**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common cause of early failure (5 years) at somewhere between 25%-45.3%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Stress fractures**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "always involve tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "associated with high activity and patient weight",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "clinically there will be a pain free interval followed by spontaneous pain with activity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "blood commonly found on joint aspiration",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "risk factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "penetrating posterior tibial cortex with guide pin, placing guide pin medial in periphery, re-drilling for guide pin, and under-sized tibial component",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Intra-operative fractures**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with forceful impacting of implant",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Outcomes",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fixed-bearing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1st decade results",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "10-year survivorship from studies done in 1980s and 1990s ranges from 87.4% to 96%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "the standard faliure rate in the first decade is 1%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "2nd decade results",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rapid decline in survivorship ranging from 79% to 90%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mobile-bearing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "excellent clinical results with 15-year survivorship reported at 93%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Long-term results",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lateral compartment arthroplasties have equivalent results to medial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "revision rates are worse than total knee revision rates",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Patellofemoral arthroplasty (PFA) has good outcomes for isolated patellofemoral arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Previous generation designs (i.e. inlay style) exhibited high rates of patellar instability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Newer generation designs (i.e. outlay style) replaces entire anterior trochlear surface and minimizes risk of patellar instability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Long term mode of failure remains progression of tibiofemoral arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "causes of late failure (>5 years)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "progress of osteoarthritis (idiopathic, over-correction, more common with mobile-bearing)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "component failure (overload due to under-correction)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "component loosening (common in fixed-bearing)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "patella impingement on femoral component (patella pain)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "polyethylene wear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
